Phase 0 smoke test — operator-sdk + kind + OLM toolchain validation
=====================================================================

1. Installed operator-sdk v1.42.3 via `brew install operator-sdk`
2. Deleted pre-existing `kind` and `k3d` (k3s-default) clusters
3. Created fresh kind cluster: `kind create cluster --name fleetdb`
4. Installed OLM 0.28.0: `operator-sdk olm install`
   - CRDs installed: catalogsources, clusterserviceversions, installplans,
     olmconfigs, operatorconditions, operatorgroups, operators, subscriptions
   - Deployments rolled out: olm-operator, catalog-operator, packageserver (2 replicas)
   - CatalogSource `operatorhubio-catalog` created in `olm` namespace
5. Scaffolded a throwaway "hello-operator" project to smoke-test the full
   dev loop (scaffold -> build -> deploy -> reconcile):
   - `operator-sdk init --domain=example.com --repo=github.com/example/hello-operator`
   - `operator-sdk create api --group=demo --version=v1alpha1 --kind=Hello --resource --controller`
   - `make manifests`
   - `make docker-build IMG=hello-operator:smoke-test`
   - `kind load docker-image hello-operator:smoke-test --name fleetdb`
   - `make install` (CRD applied)
   - `make deploy IMG=hello-operator:smoke-test`
6. Verified:
   - controller-manager pod reached Running (1/1)
   - leader election succeeded
   - controller started watching Hello CRs
   - applying config/samples/demo_v1alpha1_hello.yaml created hello-sample with no errors
7. Deleted scratch/hello-operator — served its purpose, not needed going forward.

Result: toolchain confirmed healthy end-to-end before writing any FleetDB code.
